        <div id="post-1087" class="post-1087 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized tag-code">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/2012/04/better-than-your-average-programmer/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Better than your average programmer&hellip;">Better than your average programmer&hellip;</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Apr</span>
            <span class="day">5</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/category/uncategorized/" title="View all posts in Uncategorized" rel="category tag">Uncategorized</a> | <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/2012/04/better-than-your-average-programmer/#comments" class="comments"  title="Comment on Better than your average programmer&hellip;"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="1087 http://cromwellhaus.com/?p=1087">5 Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>There was a minor discussion about enums, constants and branching on a project discussion forum recently.&#160; Alternative options suggested included polymorphism, delegate hashes and factories.&#160; One of the responses suggested these were beyond “the average programmer”. &#160; That’s crazy talk that leads straight to the ivory-tower. We just need to expose people to the alternatives [...]</p>

